    "the positive audit is now the bounded REAL ROM calibration on the copied source world and the guarded-restored experiment copy: real fixture geometry, real player, one press, a natural cart exit through the output plane and a natural void removal (no platform, no kill substitute)",
    "a like-for-like no-mod control run on the same copied world produced the same note step and removal (parity), and hook_overhead_ms now comes from the raw audit hook counters",
    "devcap failure flags come from real build/load/dependency probes; memory_state_rebuilt_after_restart comes from a post-restart snapshot/verify of the machine entities; the tool environment is derived from the harness preflight; instance isolation comes from real restart/state probes and a refused conflicting provision",
    "the unverified negative now exercises a verification-disabled restore (replace_existing + verify=false) and asserts verdict=unverified, verified=false",
    "the fixture map slice uses this run's three live initializations (captured 09:19-09:21 local) and the final run's records; the source child verdict/log sha is pinned and validated",
    "the source world is observed before and after separately and both equal the documented baseline",
    "the canonical audit rows keep the real server tick, the raw append sequence, the session and wall clock (never tick=index), and the audit lifecycle is derived from the raw events plus the flushed status",
    "trace joins now require a causal receipt (call start <= wall < next recorded call) or a bounded tick chain from a verified input; read commands, ambiguous windows, cross-scope events and out-of-bound chains fail closed, with regressions",
    "identity is measured on the restored machine with the player parked on the hover seat: a real block hit on the note block and a real type=miss after looking away",
    "the driver source hash is pinned in the run facts"
  ],
